@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Future communications. Make communications independent from core and record per-user/multiple-account consent and no admin mail-reading authority.
title AFTER MVP — independent private communications system
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190
actor "Consenting user\nOwn personal Google accounts; multiple possible" as U
rectangle "Resumefolio core" as CORE
package "Independent private communications system\nPhysical deployment / mechanisms not selected" as COM #F8EBD7 {
 component "Private mail / calendar entry\nCurrent user/account/operation authority" as E
 component "Scoped provider adapters / bounded processing" as W
 database "Private consent / account / intent / mapping records" as DB
 E --> W : explicit reviewed intent
 E --> DB : own private state
}
cloud "Gmail / Google Calendar\nPer-account consent and actual provider authority" as G
U --> E : connect own selected accounts
CORE <--> E : authenticated user-scoped API\nassociations convey no private access
W --> G : selected-account capability only
note bottom of COM
 Owner/admin role NEVER grants reading users' mail.
 Other providers remain unresolved. No MVP integration promised.
end note
@enduml
